From: kevinzhow <kevinzhow@local>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 21:29:00 +0800
Subject: PulseAudio sink: the hardware buffer size is the target latency,
 not the maximum

startStream() set maxlength to 1024 frames and left tlength to the server. A server whose sink
renders blocks larger than that (a tunnel sink renders whatever its remote may take) underruns the
stream on every block: 62 zero samples per 1024 through the Android tunnel. The size is now tlength,
with maxlength negotiated. Reproduced and checked with plasma/diagnostics/media-probes/pa-gap.py;
a server-side block limit does not cure it (docs/73).

Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-09-27
X-Rungic-Status: Pending [a plain bug; Qt 6.11.2 still sets the same attributes]
X-Rungic-Tests: L3:audio.playback (smoke); probe:plasma/diagnostics/media-probes/pa-gap.py
X-Rungic-Docs: docs/48 docs/73
---
 src/multimedia/pulseaudio/qpulseaudiosink.cpp | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/multimedia/pulseaudio/qpulseaudiosink.cpp b/src/multimedia/pulseaudio/qpulseaudiosink.cpp
index 4acf554..3ee92a5 100644
--- a/src/multimedia/pulseaudio/qpulseaudiosink.cpp
+++ b/src/multimedia/pulseaudio/qpulseaudiosink.cpp
@@ -244,8 +244,11 @@ void QPulseAudioSinkStream::uninstallCallbacks()
 bool QPulseAudioSinkStream::startStream(StreamType streamType)
 {
     pa_buffer_attr attr{
-        .maxlength = uint32_t(m_format.bytesForFrames(m_hardwareBufferFrames.value_or(1024))),
-        .tlength = uint32_t(-1),
+        // Negotiate a target latency, not a hard maximum below the server's
+        // render quantum. A tunnel may consume a block larger than 1024 frames;
+        // capping maxlength at 1024 inserts silence after every such block.
+        .maxlength = uint32_t(-1),
+        .tlength = uint32_t(m_format.bytesForFrames(m_hardwareBufferFrames.value_or(1024))),
         .prebuf = uint32_t(-1),
         .minreq = uint32_t(-1),
         .fragsize = uint32_t(-1),
